<p>In the latest development in the U.S.-Israeli war with Iran, President Trump sent mixed signals about how close the campaign is to ending. At different moments he called it “very complete” and suggested it could end “very soon,” while also warning the U.S. could strike Iran harder if Tehran disrupts energy flows. A central pressure point remains the Strait of Hormuz and Gulf shipping. Trump said the U.S. could escort tankers if needed, and separately said he would waive some oil-related sanctions to boost supply and cool prices. Iran’s Revolutionary Guards, meanwhile, said they would not allow “one litre of oil” to be shipped from the Middle East while U.S. and Israeli attacks continue—signaling that any easing of disruption hinges on an end to the strikes. Several outlets also reported Trump discussed a “quick” end to the war in a call with Russian President Vladimir Putin, even as Tehran said it would decide the war’s end on its own terms. Even with fighting ongoing, markets briefly caught their breath. Oil prices fell and some stock indexes rebounded after Trump’s remarks raised hopes—however tentative—of a shorter conflict and steadier energy supplies.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/eC3XAHqYytlhT2WbhPPa62NKBdjwIozS3I8W4xcVUUNpIFisU_XvNrFo8OgzQBWtYeAOKJl4tXizfVuJhU6_tl4nSHg1lnNgO7dHxxNPK6b8lE_SX4_U5OGen_CI_SIr_gAZZVQcdEbBzRaTfyaRmvOayLw3_muHmCKHYQmjyXLFetO5E36ff62X-GiNRuBuFnE' alt='Oil tankers anchored off Muscat, Oman, amid fears of disruptions in the Strait of Hormuz.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Escalation warning: Trump said the U.S. would hit Iran “20 times harder” if Tehran disrupts oil flows or tries to block exports.</li><li>Hormuz control rhetoric: Separate reports said Trump floated taking over or controlling the Strait of Hormuz if Iran tries “anything cute,” a tougher posture than simply escorting ships.</li><li>Battlefield claims: Trump said the U.S.-Israeli campaign has destroyed about 80% of Iran’s missile sites and launchers, offering that as evidence the war is close to meeting its objectives.</li><li>War framing: Some reporting said Trump has played down the scope of the conflict by calling it an “excursion,” while also saying the U.S. is saving some of its “most important” targets for later.</li><li>Rising toll: CBS reported a growing U.S. death toll alongside soaring energy prices, which Trump said would be temporary.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Trump: He shifted between saying the war was close to completion and arguing the U.S. had not “won enough.” At times he described it as an “excursion,” and he said some of the “most important” targets were being saved for later. (<a href='https://time.com/7383292/trump-iran-war-end/'>Time</a>, <a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/trump-israel-iran-war-us-to-end-very-soon/article70724671.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Iran’s Revolutionary Guards (IRGC): They said they would keep an oil blockade in place—“not one litre of oil”—while U.S. and Israeli attacks continue, directly tying energy disruption to the military campaign. (<a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/iran-says-oil-blockade-will-continue-until-attacks-end-trump-threatens-hit-harder'>Al-Monitor (Reuters)</a>)</li><li>Iran’s Foreign Ministry: Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi said Iran would keep fighting “as long as necessary” and ruled out a ceasefire under the reported conditions. (<a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/iran-rules-out-ceasefire-with-us-after-trump-said-war-will-be-over-soon-13987933.html'>Firstpost</a>)</li><li>Russia (President Vladimir Putin): Putin told Trump he wanted to be “helpful” on the Middle East war, and reporting also described proposals aimed at ending the conflict “quickly.” (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/9/trump-says-us-israeli-war-on-iran-will-be-over-very-soon'>Al Jazeera</a>, <a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/israel-iran-war-live-march-9-2026-mojtaba-khamenei-chosen-as-next-supreme-leader-missiles-fired-world-news-updates/article70720987.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Market participants: Investors took Trump’s end-soon comments as a possible de-escalation signal, but the quick moves in oil and equities showed how sensitive markets remain to any Hormuz-related headlines. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/09/business/stocks-iran-oil.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/03/09/world/iran-war-trump-israel-lebanon'>After Global Economy Shudders, Trump Zigzags on Whether War Is Nearing End</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/trump-says-war-could-be-over-soon-as-iran-rallies-behind-new-hardline-leader1'>Trump says war could be over soon as Iran rallies behind new hardline leader</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/middle-east/article/3346023/trump-and-putin-discuss-quick-ending-iran-war'>Trump holds phone call with Putin to discuss ‘quick’ ending to Iran war</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/us-iran-war-israel-stock-prices-down-oil-prices-up-despite-trump-reassurance/'>As U.S.-Israeli war with Iran intensifies, Trump says it is &quot;ahead of schedule&quot;</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/iran-protests-live-blog-trump-khamenei/33640284.html'>Trump: If Iran Disrupts Oil, US Will Hit &#x27;20 Times Harder&#x27;</a> - rferl.org</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/e6f166b1-c5a1-49bb-9dd5-2d0200f8afca'>Trump says Iran war will end ‘very soon’</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/03/09/2026/oil-prices-dip-under-100-as-trump-says-iran-war-very-complete'>Oil prices dip under $100 after Trump says Iran war &#x27;very complete&#x27;</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/iran-says-oil-blockade-will-continue-until-attacks-end-trump-threatens-hit-harder'>Iran says oil